<item>
            <title>[LU-20920] lu_site shrinker ignores its budget and drains one MDT per server</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20920</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;AffectedVersions&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Affected Versions&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every release from 2.6.0 through 2.17.0, and current master. Introduced by commit &lt;a href=&quot;https://git.whamcloud.com/?p=fs/lustre-release.git;a=commit;h=52d620153307605c54ea5cdb4fe95249d94081e6&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;52d620153307&lt;/a&gt; (&#8220;Backport shrinker changes from upstream&#8221;, 2014-04-24).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Problem&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a server holds several MDTs, the Lustre object-cache shrinker frees far more than the kernel asks for and always takes the excess from the same MDT, so one MDT per server is repeatedly emptied while its neighbour keeps a full cache.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Codeissue&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Code issue&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lu_cache_shrink_scan()&lt;/tt&gt; keeps visiting sites after &lt;tt&gt;remain&lt;/tt&gt; reaches 0 and passes 0 to the next site.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;lu_site_purge_objects()&lt;/tt&gt; with &lt;tt&gt;nr == 0&lt;/tt&gt; still takes one object per bucket (&lt;tt&gt;bnr = 0 / buckets + 1&lt;/tt&gt;). Then &lt;tt&gt;--nr&lt;/tt&gt; turns 0 into -1, the purge-all value, which it returns as the remainder. The next site is purged without limit.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Visited sites are moved to the tail and spliced back in the same order, so the list never rotates. The same MDT gets the zero budget on every callback.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The callback reports &lt;tt&gt;nr_to_scan + 1&lt;/tt&gt; freed while it freed up to 384.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Reproduction&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproduction&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MDS with two MDTs, 256 buckets per site:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
echo &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;0 0 128&quot;&lt;/span&gt; &amp;gt; /sys/kernel/debug/shrinker/lu_site-0/scan&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One scan of 128 purged 128 objects from MDT0001 and 256 from MDT0000. Eight scans purged 1024 and 2048, and the budget never moved to another site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Workloadfortheattachedgraphs&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Workload for the attached graphs&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;io500 mdtest-easy-stat and mdtest-hard-stat on an existing dataset of ~229 M + ~70 M files, 576 ranks (6 clients x 8 mounts), 4 ldiskfs MDTs on 2 MDS (two per server). Caches dropped once, then three passes back to back.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Without the fix, one MDT per server receives the zero budget on every callback and is drained, while its neighbour grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Fix&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Stop the scan once the budget is used up, so unvisited sites stay at the head of the list. Return from &lt;tt&gt;lu_site_purge_objects()&lt;/tt&gt; without purging when &lt;tt&gt;nr == 0&lt;/tt&gt;. The -1 purge-all of explicit callers is unchanged.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;With the fix&lt;/b&gt; (same workload, see attached graphs):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;One debugfs scan of 128 purges at most 128 objects. Eight scans split 512 / 512.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The cache of both MDTs of a server stay equal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
                <environment>- EL 9.7 Servers&lt;br/&gt;
- Lustre 2.17.0&lt;br/&gt;
- 2 MDTs per Server</environment>
